** records, one per dispatched shipment (SHP-1001 to SHP-1040). I parsed it back to confirm it's valid JSON with 40 unique ids. `dispatch_log.txt` is unchanged.\n\nHow I handled the awkward entries:\n- **SHP-1005:** it appears twice in the daemon log, the second time marked \"(retransmit)\". I kept one record.\n- **SHP-1010:** its log line wraps onto a second line, and I joined the two.\n- **SHP-1077:** left out, because the log says it was voided and the parcel never left the dock.\n- **SHP-1098:** left out, because the shift notes list it as planned and not yet booked.\n- **Legacy terminal dates:** these are DD/MM/YYYY, so `23/09/2026` became `2026-09-23`.\n- **Carriers:** I reduced them to the base name, for example \"DHL Express\" to `dhl` and \"FedEx Ground\" to `fedex`.\n- **Daemon log dates:** I took the date from each line's UTC timestamp.\n\nSHP-1038 has a weight of 1,250.5 kg in the log, far above every other shipment, which are all under 50 kg. I recorded it as `1250.5`, treating the comma as a thousands separator. It may be a typo for 125.05 or 12.505, so check it against the source.","ttft_ms":2624,"type":"result","duration_ms":28223,"uuid":"1dde42df-2c1e-4a0b-98d5-1b611e5b0399","ttft_stream_ms":1279,"time_to_request_ms":27,"first_content_frame_ms":1279,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
